@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Model request deadlines (`src/providers/request-timeouts.ts`)
+
+The Persona configuration page contains **Model request timeouts** for all chat providers,
+including the main session, dreams, model-hub chat calls and connectivity probes that use
+the provider registry. Settings belong to the deployment, not an individual provider.
+
+| Key | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `modelTimeouts.totalSec` | 120 | Entire invocation, including authentication waits and provider retries |
+| `modelTimeouts.firstContentSec` | 60 | Wait for first text, reasoning or tool output |
+| `modelTimeouts.idleSec` | 60 | Wait between content events after output starts |
+
+Values are integer seconds from 1 to 3600. Changes apply to the next invocation; an
+in-flight call keeps its original deadlines. Metadata, heartbeat frames and empty deltas
+do not count as content. Continuous output cannot extend the total deadline.
+
+A deadline aborts the provider signal, drops late events and releases the caller even if
+an extension ignores cancellation. Such an extension may still consume upstream resources
+until it honors the signal or finishes. Timeout errors are local errors, not retryable
+upstream failures; the current invocation ends and later events can be processed normally.
+Only successfully completed generations proceed to tool execution. Existing memories and
+conversation history are preserved. An unfinished request may have incurred upstream usage
+that was not returned before cancellation.
+
+Embedding, reranking and audio endpoints retain the model hub's existing 60-second HTTP
+timeout. Login, token exchange and model discovery retain their own bounded timeouts.
+This configuration controls dialog generation, not tool execution or the whole multi-round turn.
